gh issue comment 4 -R paulzierep/metagenomic-binning-benchmark --body "## Root cause found & fixed (commit \`ec41276\`, pushed)

The watchdog log tells the exact story: the **17:35–18:41 UTC outage** was the crash-loop rate limiter (6 launches/6h) firing under the OLD one-shot-per-cron design — and \`opencode run --auto\` is a SINGLE-TURN command that exits after one assistant turn, so between restarts the agent looked 'stopped'.

Fixes:
1. **Persistent driver loop** — the watchdog now launches ONE driver that keeps calling \`opencode run --auto --session ses_…\` turn after turn on the SAME session (context carries over) until the task is done, the agent crashes, or the 8 h / 200-turn budget is hit. flock guarantees a single driver; the next cron tick just skips while it is alive.
2. **Crash-guard markers only count FAILED launches** — healthy steady-state relaunches never accumulate, so the rate limiter can no longer take down a working agent.
3. **Model is now reported in the logs** — watchdog.log logs \`model=<id>\` per driver turn (incl. free-model rotation picks); \`status/current.md\` and \`status/status.log\` show the actual model in use (parsed from the transcript; currently \`big-pickle\`); the README banner + current.md keep a live status line every tick.
4. **Supervisor layer** (\`scripts/meta-watchdog.sh\`, cron */10) monitors the watchers + GitHub issues and escalates with full transcripts pushed under \`status/meta/\`.

Current: agent alive (heartbeat fresh), baseline run at epoch ~108/200. Both watchdogs + heartbeat are cron-checked every 5/10 min." 2>&1 | tail -2
