## Small dataset ready + both new directives addressed

**Small dataset (built):** `/vol/data/datasets/comebin_small` (94 MB) — top-300 contigs by length from the demo BATS metagenome (marker-gene carrying) + all reads overlapping them via `bedtools intersect -abam … -b contigs.bed -u` (params changeable). Test runner `scripts/run_small_test.sh` writes full run bookkeeping (run_meta + command lines, comebin_run.log, resources sampler). The test-run itself is queued behind the in-progress baseline run (CPU policy: no concurrent timed runs) — results will be posted here right after.

**Directive 1 — functional tests always on small data, benchmarks only after major commits:** recorded in `docs/07-fix-batches.md` + `docs/08` and adopted as the workflow: every fix batch / new version is validated on `comebin_small` (minutes, logged as usual); full timed benchmark + CheckM2/CheckM eval only for major commits.

**Directive 2 — dataset & disk-space plan incl. human host-associated data:** `docs/08-dataset-space-plan.md`. Summary: 492 GB volume, **391 GB free** now; planned additions ≈ demo 6.4 + small 0.1 + CAMI II marine (1–2 samples, 10–20 GB) + **human host-associated CAMI II** (Multisample Human Microbiome Project DOI 10.4126/frl01-006425518, or Toy Human Microbiome — 49 samples across 5 body sites; plan 1–2 samples ≤ 30 GB) + CAMI III (≤ 50 GB, sizes verified before download) ≈ **≤ 100 GB total → fits with >50 GB headroom**. Cleanup policy: delete source archives after md5/gzip-verified extraction, keep provenance (md5 + listings) in docs.
---COMMENT (by paulzierep @ 2026-09-23T19:19:23Z)---
## Supervisor follow-up: explicit medium stage + safe test runner

Acknowledged the **18:51 UTC edit**. The workflow is now explicitly:

1. run/log the real-pipeline functional test on the 94 MB small set;
2. after that passes, build/run a medium derived benchmark (initial target 3,000 contigs, hard cap 5 GB, with measured provenance/size);
3. reserve the large benchmark for post-major-commit runs.

This is now recorded in `docs/06-benchmark-commands.md`, `docs/07-fix-batches.md`, and `docs/08-dataset-space-plan.md`.

Supervisor commit `899f7e7` also closes runner gaps found during verification: `run_small_test.sh` now refuses overlap/overwrite, supports either the pristine or v1.1.0 source, passes safe CPU/seed/small-batch parameters, records the promised 30-second resource timeline, and hands off atomically to the benchmark watchdog. `run_eval.sh` refuses to overlap the registered benchmark.

No small end-to-end result is being claimed yet, and the medium set has intentionally **not** been built while the active baseline is running. Those remain gated on the small COMEBin + CheckM2/CheckM run.
